[{:db/id 17592186203933 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5678787f-ddbb-5c28-abd5-08d5ea9f1942" "question-d7920e3b-ba93-57c2-9dd2-0e80e521ff6c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203673 :question/problem "Consider the following false statement.\n\nIf $2a \\equiv 2b \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:4),$ then $a \\equiv b \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:4)$ for any $a,b \\in \\mathbb{Z}.$ \n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be a pair of integers $a$ and $b$ such that \n\n$$\n\\bbox[3px, border: 2px solid black]{\\phantom{RRR} }\\, (\\textrm{mod}\\:4) \n\\qquad\\textrm{and}\\qquad\n\\bbox[3px, border: 2px solid black]{\\phantom{RRR} }\\,  (\\textrm{mod}\\:4).\n$$\n\nFind the missing expressions." :question/worked-solution "By denoting $P(a)$ and $Q(a)$ as\n\n- $P(a,b){:} \\quad 2a \\equiv 2b \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:4)$\n\n- $Q(a,b){:} \\quad a \\equiv b \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:4)$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n\\forall a,b \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\: P \\Rightarrow Q.\n$$\n\nSince this statement is false, its negation is true.\n\nA *counterexample* is a particular case that disproves the statement. Equivalently, it's a case that proves the negation is true.\n\nThe negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀a,b\\in Z,\\,P⇒Q) & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,¬(P⇒Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,¬(¬P∨Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,P∧¬Q \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,(2a≡2b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4))\\,∧\\,(a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be a pair of integers $a$ and $b$ such that\n\n$$\n\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2a \\equiv 2b} \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:4) \n\\qquad\\textrm{and}\\qquad\n\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}a \\not\\equiv b} \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:4).\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203934 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-db63c74b-9d62-5b22-9fe0-003a0ca7d1b1" "question-d1cc0610-ee4b-58b1-8b76-c910ff50a754"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203671 :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\nFor any $a \\in \\mathbb{Z},$ if $4 \\mid a$ and $6 \\mid a,$ then $24 \\mid a.$" :question/worked-solution "By denoting $P(a),$ $Q(a),$ and $R(a)$ as\n\n- $P(a){:} \\quad 4 \\mid a$\n\n- $Q(a){:} \\quad 6 \\mid a$\n\n- $R(a){:} \\quad 24 \\mid a$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n\\forall a \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\:(P \\land Q) \\Rightarrow R.\n$$\n\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀a\\in Z,\\,(P∧Q)⇒R) & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,¬((P∧Q)⇒R) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,¬(¬(P∧Q)∨R) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,(P∧Q)∧¬R \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,P∧Q∧¬R \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,(4∣a)\\,∧\\,(6∣a)\\,∧\\,(24∤a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. \nIn other words, we need to show that there exists an integer $a$ such that \n\n$$\n4 \\mid a\n\\qquad\\textrm{and}\\qquad\n6 \\mid a  \n\\qquad\\textrm{and}\\qquad\n24 \\not\\mid a.\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $a=12$ suffices. \n\nLet's choose $a =12.$\nThen, we have that \n\n$$\n4 \\mid 12\n\\qquad\\textrm{and}\\qquad\n6 \\mid 12\n\\qquad\\textrm{and}\\qquad\n24 \\not\\mid 12.\n$$\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, $a=12$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203935 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-02cf0cdd-dd4e-5a78-a0c4-272aec9af99d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186203674 :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\nFor any $a,b \\in \\mathbb{Z},$ if $3a \\equiv 3b \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:6),$ then $a \\equiv b \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:6).$" :question/worked-solution "By denoting $P(a,b)$ and $Q(a,b)$ as\n\n- $P(a,b){:} \\quad 3a \\equiv 3b \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:6)$\n\n- $Q(a,b){:} \\quad a \\equiv b \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:6)$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n\\forall a,b \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\: P \\Rightarrow Q.\n$$\n\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀a,b\\in Z,\\,P⇒Q) & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,¬(P⇒Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,¬(¬P∨Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,P∧¬Q \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,(3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6))\\,∧\\,(a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. \nIn other words, we need to show that there exist integers $a$ and $b$ such that \n\n$$\n3a \\equiv 3b \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:6) \n\\qquad\\textrm{and}\\qquad\na \\not\\equiv b\\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:6).\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $(a,b) =(0,2)$ suffices. \n\nLet's choose\n\n$$\na = 0, \\qquad\nb = 2.\n$$\n\nThen, $3a=0$ and $3b=6.$ \n\nTo check that this is a required counterexample, we proceed as follows:\n\nHence, we have that \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{0}_{3a} \\equiv \\underbrace{6}_{3b} \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:6)\n\\qquad\\textrm{and}\\qquad\n\\underbrace{0}_{a} \\not\\equiv \\underbrace{2}_{b} \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\:6).\n$$\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, the pair $a=0$ and $b=2$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-5678787f-ddbb-5c28-abd5-08d5ea9f1942" :question/id #uuid "5678787f-ddbb-5c28-abd5-08d5ea9f1942" :question/math-academy-id "q-221959" :question/problem "Consider the following false statement.\n\nIf $a<b$ then $3a-1<2b+10$ for any $a\\in Z.$\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $a$ such that \n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{{field-2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By denoting $P(a)$ and $Q(a)$ as\n\n- $P(a):\\,a<b$\n\n- $Q(a):\\,3a-1<2b+10$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀a\\in Z,\\,P⇒Q.\n$$\n\nA *counterexample* is a particular case that disproves the statement. Equivalently, it's a case that proves the negation is true.\n\nThe negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀a\\in Z,\\,P⇒Q) & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,¬(P⇒Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,¬(¬P∨Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,P∧¬Q \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,(a<b)\\,∧\\,(3a-1\\ge 2b+10).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $a$ such that \n\n$$\na<b\\,\\text{and}\\,3a-1\\ge 2b+10.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dc8ea50c-7960-5c8e-8b36-eeb9d466fff3" "answer-field-a3d1962b-4142-509c-9371-2423b6456a30"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dc8ea50c-7960-5c8e-8b36-eeb9d466fff3" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc8ea50c-7960-5c8e-8b36-eeb9d466fff3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-eda59ec8-35cd-5dd6-af3f-e5afcd5000d1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-de7f6e29-7603-5a30-8a2a-41f42f815de4" "answer-eda59ec8-35cd-5dd6-af3f-e5afcd5000d1" "answer-c68ef504-46c3-525c-a1b8-07db1530ac37"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de7f6e29-7603-5a30-8a2a-41f42f815de4" :answer/id #uuid "de7f6e29-7603-5a30-8a2a-41f42f815de4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3a-1<2b+10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eda59ec8-35cd-5dd6-af3f-e5afcd5000d1" :answer/id #uuid "eda59ec8-35cd-5dd6-af3f-e5afcd5000d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a<b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c68ef504-46c3-525c-a1b8-07db1530ac37" :answer/id #uuid "c68ef504-46c3-525c-a1b8-07db1530ac37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a\\ge b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a3d1962b-4142-509c-9371-2423b6456a30" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d1962b-4142-509c-9371-2423b6456a30" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-b0e722e4-ead7-50ff-9f49-951697330a55" :answer-field/choices ["answer-344ee685-7c3d-57e1-8457-9b0689210e66" "answer-b0e722e4-ead7-50ff-9f49-951697330a55" "answer-a5106851-b395-588c-905c-ad9005c512b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-344ee685-7c3d-57e1-8457-9b0689210e66" :answer/id #uuid "344ee685-7c3d-57e1-8457-9b0689210e66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3a-1<2b+10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0e722e4-ead7-50ff-9f49-951697330a55" :answer/id #uuid "b0e722e4-ead7-50ff-9f49-951697330a55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3a-1\\ge 2b+10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5106851-b395-588c-905c-ad9005c512b8" :answer/id #uuid "a5106851-b395-588c-905c-ad9005c512b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a\\ge b" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d7920e3b-ba93-57c2-9dd2-0e80e521ff6c" :question/id #uuid "d7920e3b-ba93-57c2-9dd2-0e80e521ff6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-221724" :question/problem "Consider the following false statement.\n\nIf $3∣a,$ then $6∣a$ for any $a\\in Z.$\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $a$ such that \n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{{field-2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "By denoting $P(a)$ and $Q(a)$ as\n\n- $P(a):\\,3∣a$\n\n- $Q(a):\\,6∣a$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀a\\in Z,\\,P⇒Q.\n$$\n\nA *counterexample* is a particular case that disproves the statement. Equivalently, it's a case that proves the negation is true.\n\nThe negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀a\\in Z,\\,P⇒Q) & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,¬(P⇒Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,¬(¬P∨Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,P∧¬Q \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,(3∣a)\\,∧\\,(6∤a).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $a$ such that \n\n$$\n3∣a\\,\\text{and}\\,6∤a.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-612421c3-9ef7-51ac-9c53-676106d03320" "answer-field-ad76e8a7-4f4a-5af2-bba2-21dbd8fbcccd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-612421c3-9ef7-51ac-9c53-676106d03320" :answer-field/id #uuid "612421c3-9ef7-51ac-9c53-676106d03320" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-66ba3587-ad47-5715-bd71-005204af28b9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-66ba3587-ad47-5715-bd71-005204af28b9" "answer-a4478efe-25df-5213-8187-f598d3ce28e1" "answer-b7cdc3b5-e873-53de-8e6b-fd925dbe49a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66ba3587-ad47-5715-bd71-005204af28b9" :answer/id #uuid "66ba3587-ad47-5715-bd71-005204af28b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3∣a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4478efe-25df-5213-8187-f598d3ce28e1" :answer/id #uuid "a4478efe-25df-5213-8187-f598d3ce28e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3∤a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7cdc3b5-e873-53de-8e6b-fd925dbe49a3" :answer/id #uuid "b7cdc3b5-e873-53de-8e6b-fd925dbe49a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6∣a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ad76e8a7-4f4a-5af2-bba2-21dbd8fbcccd" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad76e8a7-4f4a-5af2-bba2-21dbd8fbcccd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-387ccfaa-cabf-5956-8fb7-c24ffe7d7868" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f34a320d-4941-51b7-bd57-825b87bc6011" "answer-2f9b9d97-f210-5e3f-9eac-9541bfee4624" "answer-387ccfaa-cabf-5956-8fb7-c24ffe7d7868"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f34a320d-4941-51b7-bd57-825b87bc6011" :answer/id #uuid "f34a320d-4941-51b7-bd57-825b87bc6011" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3∤a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f9b9d97-f210-5e3f-9eac-9541bfee4624" :answer/id #uuid "2f9b9d97-f210-5e3f-9eac-9541bfee4624" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6∣a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-387ccfaa-cabf-5956-8fb7-c24ffe7d7868" :answer/id #uuid "387ccfaa-cabf-5956-8fb7-c24ffe7d7868" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6∤a" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-db63c74b-9d62-5b22-9fe0-003a0ca7d1b1" :question/id #uuid "db63c74b-9d62-5b22-9fe0-003a0ca7d1b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-221738" :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\nFor any $a\\in Z,$ if $15∣6a,$ then $15∣a.$\n\nTo {{field-1}} a universal statement, it's sufficient to find {{field-2}}. \nIn other words, we need to show that {{field-3}}\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nLet's choose $a=$ {{field-6}}.\nThen, we have that \n\n$$\n15{{field-7}}{{30}_{⏟}}_{6a}\\,\\text{and}\\,15{{field-8}}{{5}_{⏟}}_{a}.\n$$\n\nSo, $a=$ {{field-9}} is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/worked-solution "By denoting $P(a)$ and $Q(a)$ as\n\n- $P(a):\\,15∣6a$\n\n- $Q(a):\\,15∣a$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀a\\in Z,\\,P⇒Q.\n$$\n\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀a\\in Z,\\,P⇒Q) & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,¬(P⇒Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,¬(¬P∨Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,P∧¬Q \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,(15∣6a)\\,∧\\,(15∤a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. \nIn other words, we need to show that there exists an integer $a$ such that \n\n$$\n15∣6a\\,\\text{and}\\,15∤a.\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $a=5$ suffices. \n\nLet's choose $a=5.$\nThen, we have that \n\n$$\n15∣{{30}_{⏟}}_{6a}\\,\\text{and}\\,15∤{{5}_{⏟}}_{a}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, $a=5$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-73ec0225-f537-55df-a931-0499d34c0141" "answer-field-648de8d0-1abf-5247-8526-b6083fc53110" "answer-field-9d9cba76-6933-5ee2-8dc9-ba097e1d10e7" "answer-field-83515bfa-b582-5f53-b213-0aedfae18b90" "answer-field-3936e0ea-927d-5098-a33d-5088fa2ab3ba" "answer-field-4fcbc108-7d3e-5abf-b1e7-d2a6883fb96d" "answer-field-8c13378a-a3b4-5489-85b7-0835caa4bb41" "answer-field-7e6dec42-e66c-52e1-9d3d-1655fa42b33c" "answer-field-6c0a53af-037d-56cb-a78f-36b8cc053489"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-73ec0225-f537-55df-a931-0499d34c0141" :answer-field/id #uuid "73ec0225-f537-55df-a931-0499d34c0141" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-8fbd6c13-44b9-5665-ac20-baf0a39b1ae1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8fbd6c13-44b9-5665-ac20-baf0a39b1ae1" "answer-7b4e175b-f196-54a5-9f20-7bd223b7d990"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8fbd6c13-44b9-5665-ac20-baf0a39b1ae1" :answer/id #uuid "8fbd6c13-44b9-5665-ac20-baf0a39b1ae1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "disprove" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b4e175b-f196-54a5-9f20-7bd223b7d990" :answer/id #uuid "7b4e175b-f196-54a5-9f20-7bd223b7d990" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "prove" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-648de8d0-1abf-5247-8526-b6083fc53110" :answer-field/id #uuid "648de8d0-1abf-5247-8526-b6083fc53110" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-69b22aaf-0b8c-596b-8fba-030a4d29beda" :answer-field/choices ["answer-69b22aaf-0b8c-596b-8fba-030a4d29beda" "answer-5d3d5e6d-5ac8-52ea-a7a3-16c8b46c32a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69b22aaf-0b8c-596b-8fba-030a4d29beda" :answer/id #uuid "69b22aaf-0b8c-596b-8fba-030a4d29beda" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a counterexample" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d3d5e6d-5ac8-52ea-a7a3-16c8b46c32a5" :answer/id #uuid "5d3d5e6d-5ac8-52ea-a7a