-56cb-a78f-36b8cc053489" :answer-field/key "field-9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c68769eb-fc15-5f82-8e39-5f874f29cf33" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ecc904e9-f99f-55c4-9491-aa5e7f676a98" "answer-6144e55b-3568-59c7-bf79-7172d83fe07e" "answer-c68769eb-fc15-5f82-8e39-5f874f29cf33" "answer-cc33c8d7-f862-5dee-b24e-6b77925a0889"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ecc904e9-f99f-55c4-9491-aa5e7f676a98" :answer/id #uuid "ecc904e9-f99f-55c4-9491-aa5e7f676a98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6144e55b-3568-59c7-bf79-7172d83fe07e" :answer/id #uuid "6144e55b-3568-59c7-bf79-7172d83fe07e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c68769eb-fc15-5f82-8e39-5f874f29cf33" :answer/id #uuid "c68769eb-fc15-5f82-8e39-5f874f29cf33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc33c8d7-f862-5dee-b24e-6b77925a0889" :answer/id #uuid "cc33c8d7-f862-5dee-b24e-6b77925a0889" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d1cc0610-ee4b-58b1-8b76-c910ff50a754" :question/id #uuid "d1cc0610-ee4b-58b1-8b76-c910ff50a754" :question/math-academy-id "q-221742" :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\nFor any $a\\in Z,$ if $10∣a$ and $15∣a,$ then $150∣a.$\n\nTo {{field-1}} a universal statement, it's sufficient to find {{field-2}}. \nIn other words, we need to show that {{field-3}}\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{{field-5}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{{field-6}}.\n$$\n\nLet's choose $a=$ {{field-7}}.\nThen, we have that \n\n$$\n10{{field-8}}30\\,\\text{and}\\,15{{field-9}}30\\,\\text{and}\\,150{{field-10}}30.\n$$\n\nSo, $a=$ {{field-11}} is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/worked-solution "By denoting $P(a),$ $Q(a),$ and $R(a)$ as\n\n- $P(a):\\,10∣a$\n\n- $Q(a):\\,15∣a$\n\n- $R(a):\\,150∣a$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀a\\in Z,\\,(P∧Q)⇒R.\n$$\n\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀a\\in Z,\\,(P∧Q)⇒R) & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,¬((P∧Q)⇒R) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,¬(¬(P∧Q)∨R) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,(P∧Q)∧¬R \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,P∧Q∧¬R \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,(10∣a)\\,∧\\,(15∣a)\\,∧\\,(150∤a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. \nIn other words, we need to show that there exists an integer $a$ such that \n\n$$\n10∣a\\,\\text{and}\\,15∣a\\,\\text{and}\\,150∤a.\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $a=30$ suffices. \n\nLet's choose $a=30.$\nThen, we have that \n\n$$\n10∣30\\,\\text{and}\\,15∣30\\,\\text{and}\\,150∤30.\n$$\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, $a=30$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-605bde41-5797-5efa-814b-4ffed494727d" "answer-field-002d46cf-e110-5bd6-aff7-940eea1468e5" "answer-field-14d34f2e-abf2-5b37-b639-50fdc4f3bd00" "answer-field-acda9280-4e82-530b-aa68-a21a28710c4d" "answer-field-08cb0952-5dd2-5a60-a191-94672e4791c9" "answer-field-23bec174-4de9-51f0-a50e-cf54fb397a84" "answer-field-ba306d62-71ef-55ce-a9af-0cbacbe45975" "answer-field-be9ca723-cff2-5337-9476-0020a32363b3" "answer-field-14bf9ef7-1bf2-5437-95ac-10bebbd4f3e4" "answer-field-bac48d4d-c6a3-5c77-93f2-6a947e9b0f02" "answer-field-0e7aebca-d675-578f-bd3e-8053463fe23e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-605bde41-5797-5efa-814b-4ffed494727d" :answer-field/id #uuid "605bde41-5797-5efa-814b-4ffed494727d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-0a0fe9e2-878f-5dcb-9cbb-204fea3a1e28" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0a0fe9