answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebbd4763-dc95-5f79-a5ba-c3b36ef82fad" :answer/id #uuid "ebbd4763-dc95-5f79-a5ba-c3b36ef82fad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "300" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-02cf0cdd-dd4e-5a78-a0c4-272aec9af99d" :question/id #uuid "02cf0cdd-dd4e-5a78-a0c4-272aec9af99d" :question/math-academy-id "q-221751" :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\nFor any $a,b\\in Z,$ if $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2),$ then $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).$\n\nTo {{field-1}} a universal statement, it's sufficient to find {{field-2}}. \nIn other words, we need to show that {{field-3}}\n\n$$\n{{field-4}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nLet's choose\n\n$$\na={{field-6}},\\,b={{field-7}}.\n$$\n\nHence, we have that \n\n$$\n0{{field-8}}2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\,\\text{and}\\,0{{field-9}}2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$\n\nSo, the pair $a=$ {{field-10}} and $b=$ {{field-11}} is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/worked-solution "By denoting $P(a,b)$ and $Q(a,b)$ as\n\n- $P(a,b):\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$\n\n- $Q(a,b):\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀a,b\\in Z,\\,P⇒Q.\n$$\n\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀a,b\\in Z,\\,P⇒Q) & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,¬(P⇒Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,¬(¬P∨Q) \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,P∧¬Q \\\\  & ≡\\,∃a,b\\in Z,\\,(a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2))\\,∧\\,(a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. \nIn other words, we need to show that there exist integers $a$ and $b$ such that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\,\\text{and}\\,a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $(a,b)=(0,2)$ suffices. \n\nLet's choose\n\n$$\na=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nTo check that this is a required counterexample, we proceed as follows:\n\nHence, we have that \n\n$$\n0≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\,\\text{and}\\,0≢2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, the pair $a=0$ and $b=2$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3486b2dd-8580-536a-af90-a429281a30c7" "answer-field-474b6012-0b43-5706-b2d3-d41671e1faa3" "answer-field-555a8aee-26b6-547c-83e3-cfe06b9bc933" "answer-field-6014d685-4834-56f0-ae23-295d2302ca29" "answer-field-67e535f6-f215-5564-ad25-d1ee7a6a2925" "answer-field-7e61d21e-a8ee-5d35-aa11-c61e72848c9b" "answer-field-8a9fd908-6794-5454-8216-727fb0467d1b" "answer-field-07151903-b835-5c9e-b334-0fecb3cbd93e" "answer-field-e5e010d1-f63c-5f6c-b952-15b68d471658" "answer-field-feca1384-ecee-53ea-9957-2c042f82b064" "answer-field-bd40404c-5720-5352-8961-0f173651d487"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3486b2dd-8580-536a-af90-a429281a30c7" :answer-field/id #uuid "3486b2dd-8580-536a-af90-a429281a30c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-d6fccf31-bc5c-58f4-9f40-51e3274806dd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d6fccf31-bc5c-58f4-9f40-51e3274806dd" "answer-ac7f4fc0-a360-566e-b07b-0d917064981e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6fccf31-bc5c-58f4-9f40-51e3274806dd" :answer/id #uuid "d6fccf31-bc5c-58f4-9f40-51e3274806dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "disprove" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac7f4fc0-a360-566e-b07b-0d917064981e" :answer/id #uuid "ac7f4fc0-a360-566e-b07b-0d917064981e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "prove" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-474b6012-0b43-5706-b2d3-d41671e1faa3" :answer-field/id #uuid "474b6012-0b43-5706-b2d3-d41671e1faa3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-fie